; watermark.aura — watermark / late-event handling for the streaming engine.
;
; The watermark represents the engine's progress in event-time. Events with a
; timestamp at or beyond the current watermark are considered "on time" or
; "late-but-bounded". Events whose timestamp is strictly less than the
; current watermark are "late" arrivals — they arrived after the engine
; already considered the watermark advanced past their event-time.
;
; In a real engine, late events trigger retraction: the engine looks up the
; key's current value, computes the reverse delta, and writes a retraction
; into the retract log. Here we just expose the watermark primitives the
; engine uses to decide whether an event is late.
;
; State shape: a single number — the current event-time watermark.
;
; API:
;   (wm-advance wm ts)  — return a new watermark advanced to ts if ts is
;                         strictly greater than the current watermark;
;                         otherwise return wm unchanged. (Watermarks are
;                         monotonically non-decreasing.)
;   (wm-is-late? wm ts) — return #t if ts is strictly less than the
;                         current watermark, #f otherwise.
;   (wm-current wm)     — return the current watermark value.

; Advance the watermark to the given event-time, if it is strictly greater
; than the current watermark. Watermarks only move forward.
(define (api wm-advance wm ts)
  (if (> ts wm) ts wm))

; Is the given event-time a late arrival relative to the current watermark?
; An event is late iff its timestamp is strictly less than the watermark.
(define (api wm-is-late? wm ts)
  (if (< ts wm) #t #f))

; Return the current watermark value.
(define (api wm-current wm)
  wm)
